    "name": "Owning things",
    "template": "possessor base  +  -a / -i / -e   —   the OWNED thing decides the ending",
    "notes": [
      "The owned thing decides the ending, not the owner: mer + a / i / e.",
      "Same base, two systems: -ko = wanting (to them) · -ka / -ki / -ke = owning (their).",
      "Decoding \"her laptop\": \"her\" picks the base by distance and respect (is / us / in / un); \"laptop\" picks the ending (electronic = masculine = -ka). Near = iska laptop, far = uska laptop. Two decisions, one word."
